      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Tempest Temple [zone=1015]\n**Who:**\n- Ognit Eznertob [npc=47704]\nRating:\n0/1**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\n(From 1 rating)\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 95\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Aged Metal [item=120491]\n- Storm Scroll [item=120490]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Tempest Temple: Clearer Skies [zone=1024]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Bindess Lon [npc=48367]\n- Kelpin Larch [npc=48368]\n- Krinoch Jal [npc=48369]\n- Ognit Eznertob [npc=48370]\n- a chest - Clearer Skies [npc=48686]\n- a conjured storm [npc=48363]\n- a cursed evoker [npc=47832]\n- a cursed pirate [npc=47833]\n- a storm totem [npc=48364]\n- a tempest evoker [npc=47859]\n- a tempest keeper [npc=47860]\n- a totem disruptor [npc=48365]\n- a totem guard [npc=48366]\n**Related Quests:**\n- TDS Progression #0: An Overview [quest=7701]\n- TDS Progression #2: Gathering Clouds [quest=7703]\n- TDS Progression #4a: The Pellarus Satum [quest=7705]\n- TDS Progression #4b: The Edge of Balance [quest=7706]\n**Era:** | !The Darkened Sea\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 3\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Sun Oct 26 02:51:45 2014\nModified: Thu Sep 19 06:45:49 2024 |\n---\n\n**The Darkened Sea Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\nThis group mission begins with Ognit Eznertob ( **click for map image**), who is located on the eastern coast of the island.\n_Pre-requisites for requesting:_\n\\- Completion of \"A Rising Storm\"\n\\- Completion of \"Gathering Clouds\"\n_Say \"scrolls\" to request the task._\n_At the end of the previous task, you saw:_\nOgnit Eznertob says 'Brother Minkins is...? On the voyage he kept telling us sirens could be lurking anywhere. I suppose he finally found them.' Ognit takes the tools and looks thoughtfully at one of the storm totems. 'Now, if I only knew more about the [spells] the kedge are using...''\nYou say, 'What spells?'\nOgnit Eznertob says 'Al`Kabor never taught me enough of all he knows. I would think Norrath's greatest wizard would have possessed even a puff of knowledge about storms. So again I am at a loss. If the kedge carry [scrolls] filled with the knowledge of storm magic, I could puzzle out their workings.'\nYou say, 'What scrolls?'\nOgnit Eznertob says 'The druids surely carry such scrolls.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Clearer Skies'.\nOgnit almost has everything he needs to combat the intense storm. Once you supply him with the rest of what he needs, you can push back the storm around the portal to Katta Castrum.\n\n---\n\nLoot storm scrolls from the kedge 0/6 (Tempest Temple)\n_Kill Kedge mobs (\"a tempest keeper\"; \"a tempest evoker\") in the center area of the island (patrolling the path through the mountain) until you've looted 6x \"Storm Scroll\". Mobs in this area hit for a max ~12,500 and tend to be immune to both stun and mez (exceptions being \"a storm dervish\" and \"an earthen dervish\")._\nGive the storm scrolls to Ognit 0/6 (Tempest Temple)\nOgnit Eznertob unrolls several scrolls and scans them quickly. 'I see that they say... well... I have no idea what these say!' Ognit tosses the scrolls on the ground in frustration. 'I really should have kept up with my studies! I'll need more time to figure out what the scrolls mean, but what I can make out so far is that I will need aged metal. There should be plenty of that in the shipwreck.\n\n---\n\nLoot aged metal pieces from the undead sailors 0/6 (Tempest Temple)\n_Head to the shipwreck off the northeast coast and kill undead until you've looted 6x \"Aged Metal\"._\nGive the aged metal pieces to Ognit 0/6 (Tempest Temple)\nOgnit Eznertob hammers, curses, casts a spell, and curses again. He holds up the altered totems. 'These should disrupt the storms. Should. I've imbued them with a calming spell that should interact with the charges in the air, and... well, I hope it's enough. We should [go] place these before the kedge know what we are up to!'\n_The next part of the task involves an instanced version of Tempest Temple. Say \"go\" to zone into the instance._\nYou say, 'Let's go...'\nOgnit Eznertob says 'We'll meet at the floating island!'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Tempest Temple Mission.\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Ognit near the floating island 0/1 (Tempest Temple)\nYou say, 'Hail, Ognit Eznertob'\nOgnit Eznertob lifts his head to the clouded sky and shields his eyes from the rain, looking at the floating rocks around the island. 'Take the disruptors. We'll head up the ramp and place them around the island. Tell me when you're ready, and I'll deliver you safely to the rocks.'\n_When ready for a fight, hail Ognit Eznertob to be ported up to the small island next to the path._\nYou say, 'Hail, Ognit Eznertob'\nOgnit Eznertob says 'Up you go!'\n\n---\n\nPlace the first disruptor and defeat the totem defenders 0/3 (Tempest Temple)\n_After a small delay, you'll see this..._\nOgnit Eznertob shouts 'Place the disruptor next to the storm totem to knock out the power of the kedge's storm!'\nKelpin Larch yells from the island ridge, 'You would make this island safe for the Combine? You would strip us of our refuge? We endured decades of suffering at their hands, and now you would return us to their clutches? One of us will die before that happens!'\n_...And 3x \"a temple guard\" spawn around the storm totem. These mobs are permanently rooted, each hit for a max ~9,500; have ~1,750,000 hitpoints; and are stunnable but are NOT mezzable. They summon when damaged, do NOT see invisibility, and are NOT auto-aggro._\n\n---\n\nPlace the second disruptor and defeat the totem defenders 0/3 (Tempest Temple)\n_Repeat as above for the next island up._\nBindess Lon joins her voice with her master's. 'You will never take our island from us! You will never subjugate us again -- not even with your most powerful beams of magic!'\n\n---\n\nPlace the third disruptor and defeat the totem defenders 0/4 (Tempest Temple)\n_Repeat as above for the next island up, except this time with one additional mob._\nKelpin Larch shouts 'Katta Castrum will drown! This island will be no refuge for the Combine! There will be no survivors!'\n\n---\n\nPlace the fourth disruptor and defeat the totem defenders 0/4 (Tempest Temple)\n_Repeat as above, again with four mobs._\nOgnit Eznertob shouts 'This is the last one!'\nBindess Lon glances worriedly at her master. 'They're still coming! May I use all you've taught me?'\nKelpin Larch shouts 'Yes, show them the resilience of the kedge!'\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Kelpin Larch 0/6 (Tempest Temple)\n**TASK LOCKS HERE**\n_Hail him until the task updates. (Be ready for a fight.)_\nKelpin Larch shouts 'Krinoch! Slink back into the sea, slave! You are not worthy to stand among free kedge! Why don't you teleport to Katta Castrum and offer yourself as a sacrifice for your beloved Tsaph Katta!'\nKrinoch Jal shouts 'No, no, I am loyal to Karana! I love the rain and the storms! So delightful on the skin!' Krinoch shivers and averts his eyes from Kelpin. 'I only want peace for us all!''\nKelpin Larch shouts 'There should be no peace for the Combine! Did you know that at one time Tsaph Katta preached of inclusiveness and the value of all races? And what of our race? To the Combine we were lower than the fish in the ocean deep. But now we have risen to the surface, and the Combine languish below the waves!'\nOgnit Eznertob holds out his palm and puffs his chest, looking as big as a gnome can. 'The storms shall cease! Return to your island and make peace, or you will have to deal with me!'\nBindess Lon laughs. 'Such big words for so small a creature! I've seen your spells, and they don't frighten me. You're no sort of wizard!' Bindess looks to Kelpin. 'Master, may I teach the gnome how to properly cast a spell?'\nKelpin Larch shouts 'A magic lesson would be beyond him. Teach the gnome how to die!'\nBindess Lon says 'Get off our isle, landling!'\nKelpin Larch shouts 'You can defeat him! He is no match for you!'\n\n---\n\nDefeat Bindess Lon 0/1 (Tempest Temple)\n_Bindess Lon isn't much harder than regular mobs here. She has ~3.9 million hitpoints and is immune to mez and stun. She casts \"Lesser Storm\" on random single targets:_\nLesser Storm: Single Target, Cold (-975)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 50000\n_Once she reaches very low health, she goes non-aggro, and Kelpin Larch attacks:_\nKelpin Larch shouts 'Bindess, no!' Kelpin rushes to the aid of his apprentice, wreathing a barrier of magic around her. 'They will not harm you!'\n\n---\n\nDefeat Kelpin Larch 0/1 (Tempest Temple)\n_Like Bindess Lon, Kelpin Larch is only a bit more difficult than the average mob here (has ~5 million hitpoints). He casts \"Greater Storm\":_\nGreater Storm: PB AE 100', Cold (-975)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 60000\n_DPS Kelpin Larch to the death._\nBindess Lon shouts 'Master, you can't die! Not to them! You're stronger than they are! Master!'\nKelpin Larch has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nKelpin Larch's corpse moans malevolently, \"We will rise... from the deep...\"\nBindess Lon says, 'Master... I followed you all those years... I followed you to freedom, to the surface... and now am I to follow you in death?' Bindess beseeches you with her eyes. 'Please don't kill me... I don't want to die yet...'\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Krinoch Jal 0/1 (Tempest Temple)\nYou say, 'Hail, Krinoch Jal'\nKrinoch Jal says 'I thought I would be the one mixing my blood with the rain...' Krinoch looks at the sky. 'The storm has diminished near the portal. Now it should be safe enough to cross through it. I don't know what's happening in Katta Castrum, but once the Combine start arriving here, my brethren might be even less amenable to words than Kelpin was.'\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Ognit 0/3 (Tempest Temple)\n_Hail him until the task completes (\"go\" will zone you out). A chest also spawns at this time. The task is repeatable with a 6-hour lockout timer from the time of request._\nOgnit Eznertob says 'Thanks to you the portal should be safer, but still the storms rage.' Ognit looks at his hands. He breathes hard. 'It's been a long time since I've been in a fight. I don't know whether to cheer or wretch... I had forgotten how it felt to see your enemy lying dead at your feet. It used to be easier. But there might be many more dead to follow.'\nOgnit Eznertob says 'Katta Castrum must be in trouble if their people are trying to come here.' Ognit looks at the volcanic island glowing brightly in the darkness. 'The beam arced above the island, but it must not have come from the kedge. And still Cecile controls the winds. I cannot yet accompany you.'\nOgnit Eznertob says 'I will wait here. I know I can't face Cecile. You saw how little I remember about magic! But I will see what can be done and help the shipwreck survivors in the meantime. [Go] in my stead. See Firiona and make sure she is safe; tell her what has happened here. If she doubts you, tell her 'the companions sail the darkened sea.' Storms and black waters lie ahead, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_.'\n_Rewards:_\n187 platinum, 5 gold\nExperience\n_Possible Chest Loot [npc=48686] (1 item + 0-1 armor template + 0-1 Briny Essence + 0-1 Valiant ornament):_\nFused Coral Staff\nReefmaw Carapace Mask\nSerpentscale Belt\nSlimy Tentacle\nStorm Scarred Ring\nCastaway Armguards\nCastaway Bracer\nCastaway Boots\nCastaway Gloves\nCastaway Helm\nCastaway Leggings\nCastaway Tunic\nMinor Briny Essence\nLesser Briny Essence\nMedian Briny Essence",
    },
