      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Tempest Temple [zone=1015]\n**Who:**\n- Jessup Stormwind [ _Quests_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 100\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Infused Coral Extract [item=120638]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- a green coral plant [npc=47836]\n- a sea naga evoker [npc=47848]\n- a sea naga stormcaller [npc=47849]\n- a small serpent [npc=47854]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Jessup #1: Coral Crushers [quest=7727]\n- Jessup #3: Bigger Fish [quest=7729]\n**Era:** | !The Darkened Sea\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Sun Oct 26 03:21:07 2014\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 |\n---\n\n**The Darkened Sea Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This solo task is the second in a series of three. It begins with Jessup Stormwind ( **click for map image**) in Tempest Temple. He is located at -340, -280, -156 (on the elevated island in the southeastern part of the zone)._\n_Pre-Requisites for Requesting:_\n\\- Completion of \"Coral Crushers\"\n_Say \"hand\" to request the task._\n_At the end of the previous task, you saw:_\nJessup Stormwind smirks as you recount the tale of goblin genocide and the state of the reef. 'Such is the justice of nature \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. Pray that you never fall victim to her ire. Though it be very odd that the green coral has not seen the same damage as the other species. I can only conclude that the goblins and the nagas have some reason for not trampling it. From the traces of magic in the coral you felt it seems likely that the hags are empowering them somehow. Though I am usually grateful for any creature that assists with the cultivation of the wild, I have a [bad feeling] about this.\nYou say, 'A bad feeling?'\nJessup Stormwind says 'The naga are clearly up to something nefarious with their magically infused coral. I can't say definitively, but I suspect it may have something to do with the rather large ocean serpents that have been wandering through the shallows lately. From prior experience I can tell you that they are decidedly larger than they ought normally to be. Perhaps the nagas are feeding them the magically infused coral. That would be odd, as the serpents normally subsist on a diet of fish and small crustaceans. Which reminds me, those crabs down below are a bit massive too aren't they? Never mind that for now, back to the matter at [hand].'\nYou say, 'What's at hand?'\nJessup Stormwind says 'Even if the nagas' motivations are altruistic, the presence of so much coral of a single species is not good for the ecology of the reef. I'm loathe to say it, but the best course of action seems to be for you to crush some of that coral. I doubt that will be enough to put an end to it though. You'll also need to thin the ranks of those nagas significantly. If you could remove them from the situation my instincts tell me that the goblins would break ranks and stop disrupting the reef. Be careful though, if any of them are using that coral for nefarious purposes you could be in for a rude awakening.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'So Many Serpents'.\nJessup Stormwind wants your help destroying some of the overabundant green coral in the shallows around the Tempest Temple. As the nagas are the source of the real problem, he also wants you to thin out their ranks and keep an eye out for anything that might provide some information about their larger plan.\nDestroy green coral plants. You'll likely attract nearby serpents when you do, so be careful.\n\n---\n\nCrush green coral plants and kill small serpents 0/5 (Tempest Temple)\nSlay several sea nagas 0/10 (Tempest Temple)\nCollect infused coral extracts from the nagas 0/3 (Tempest Temple)\n_Head back to the western part of the zone. Note that sea nagas are stunnable and rootable/snareable, but immune to mez._\n_When you 'kill' a green coral, \"a small serpent\" spawns at its location. This mob has to be killed for updates. It has less hitpoints than the average and is mezzable, stunnable, rootable, and snareable. It also flees at low health._\na green coral plant crumbles beneath your attack, as a small sea serpent emerges from the nearby water to attack!\na small serpent weaves forward with lightning speed.\n_NOTE: \"Infused Coral Extract\" is the item you're looking for. This drops from the sea nagas, but may only have a chance to drop if everyone in your group is on the same task and step. If this is the case, you can get around this issue by having anyone who does NOT have this task disband from the group before a mob dies. The item 'seed' check is at the time of death._\n\n---\n\nBring the infused coral extracts to Jessup Stormwind 0/3 (Tempest Temple)\nJessup Stormwind carefully peers through the green liquid as he taps lightly on the side of the glass vial. 'A potent growth enchantment has been cast on this coral for certain, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. They seem to have extracted all the nutrients of the coral into this liquid.' He pauses from his study of the vial to look at you before continuing, 'You say the serpents came to aid the nagas when you attacked them? This must be the reason for this new 'alliance' of sorts. This can't be the end game though. The serpents, though larger still do not pose a significant threat to the rest of the islands' inhabitants. Unless of course there's some kind of even bigger [monstrosity] that they've been feeding?'\n_Rewards:_\nExperience\n90 platinum\n_This task is repeatable with a 6-hour lockout timer from the time of request._",
    },
