      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Tempest Temple [zone=1015]\n**Who:**\n- Petran Searake [npc=47707]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 95\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Related Zones:**\n- Tempest Temple: Storm of Sorts [zone=1023]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Petran Searake [npc=48362]\n- Serisaria [npc=47679]\n- a cursed pirate [npc=48339]\n- a lava spirit [npc=48340]\n- a lost siren [npc=48341]\n- a reef crab [npc=48342]\n- a reef crawler [npc=48343]\n- a reef walker [npc=48344]\n- a sea banshee [npc=48345]\n- a sea goblin shaman [npc=48346]\n- a sea goblin warrior [npc=48347]\n- a sea naga evoker [npc=48348]\n- a sea naga stormcaller [npc=48349]\n- a storm champion [npc=48350]\n- a storm dervish [npc=48351]\n- a tempest dervish [npc=48352]\n- a tempest evoker [npc=48353]\n- a tempest keeper [npc=48354]\n- a treant guardian [npc=48355]\n- a warden of Tunare [npc=48356]\n- an air spirit [npc=48357]\n- an earthen dervish [npc=48358]\n- an enraged rocksnapper [npc=48359]\n- an ocean caller [npc=48360]\n- an ocean serpent [npc=48361]\n**Era:** | !The Darkened Sea\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Sun Oct 26 03:22:00 2014\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 |\n---\n\n**The Darkened Sea Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n**About Heroic Adventures:**\n\\- They use the task system (steps are shown in task window, but steps are only revealed as you get to them).\n\\- Scale in difficulty, loot quality, and mob levels (based on your group's highest level player - as low as 85).\n\\- Tuned for 2-3 players and their mercenaries.\n\\- Nameds can spawn as you progress through the task (you usually have to complete a few steps before this can happen).\n\\- Collection items can drop from mobs in the instances, and ground spawns appear midway through tasks.\n\\- Expected time of completion will vary by your group's makeup (anywhere from 30-90+ minutes).\n\\- There is some variations/randomization in the task steps you'll be assigned as you progress through the task.\n**About Our Documentation of Heroic Adventures**\n\\- We only display task steps we know about.\n\\-\\-\\- If you encounter a step that isn't documented here, please post the details (or email us) and **be sure to indicate which step number it was** so that we can display it in its proper place.\n\n---\n\n_This is a heroic adventure (1-6 players) that begins with Petran Searake ( **click for map image**) in Tempest Temple (located at the dock on the eastern coast)._\n_Pre-Requisites for Requesting:_\n\\- None\n\n---\n\n**TASK SUMMARY**\n\\- Say \"fish\" to request the task and \"ready\" to zone in.\n**Step #1:**\nKill the crawlers and walkers that infest the coral reef 0/18\n\\-\\-\\- Kill update.\nStop the sea goblins 0/22\n\\-\\-\\- Kill update.\nBanish the restless undead 0/20\n\\-\\-\\- Kill update.\n**Step #2:**\nSilence the hideous sea nagas 0/9\n\\-\\-\\- Kill update.\nStill the restless elementals 0/10\n\\-\\-\\- Kill update.\nDisrupt the chaotic dervishes 0/9\n\\-\\-\\- Kill update in the path in the middle of the island.\n**Step #3:**\nKill a few coral or ocean serpents 0/6\n\\-\\-\\- Kill update.\nTake out the sirens or their seduced pirates 0/6\n\\-\\-\\- Kill update.\nCrush a few reef crabs 0/6\n\\-\\-\\- Kill update.\nKnock some sense into the Wardens and their Treants 0/5\n\\-\\-\\- Kill update on the floating island. (Warning: These mobs are a lot tougher than general zone population.)\nKill 5 Kedge 0/5\n\\-\\-\\- Kill update in the path through the mountain.\n**\\- At this point in the task, collectibles spawn in the zone (ground spawns) and a named (or its PH) has a chance to spawn.**\n**Step #4:**\nSpeak to Petran Searake 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Hail update to finish.\n\n---\n\n**NAMED MOBS**\n_\"Serisaria\" (or its PH, \"a lost siren\") spawns after the third step is completed. This mob appears near the entrance to the Caverns of Endless Song (far northern part of the zone in the coral reef)._\n_Known loot from this named:_\nLevel 105\nCastaway Bracer\nFused Coral Staff\nSerisaria's Pearl Stud\nLevel 100\n???\nLevel 95\n???\nLevel 90\n???\n\n---\n\n**TASK IN DETAIL**\n========================================================================\nTRIGGERING THE TASK\n========================================================================\nYou say, 'Hail, Petran Searake'\nPetran Searake sighs, 'Seems your luck is as bad as mine, stranger. You without direction and me without a [catch].'\nYou say, 'No catch?'\nPetran Searake chuckles, 'The weather being what it is, I can't rightly expect there to be an abundance catch, but I haven't caught a [fish] in days now. I suspect what little sea life remains out there is being caught up by the miserable beasts on the isle. Interested in reducing my competition? I may not have fish but I should be able to scrounge up some suiting reward for you.'\nYou say, 'I'll get you some fish'\nPetran Searake says 'Excellent, just tell me when you're [ready] to go.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Storm of Sorts'.\nPetran Searake has had miserable luck catching any fish lately. He suspects his luck will improve if you reduce his competition around the island.\n========================================================================\nSTEP #1\n========================================================================\nKill the crawlers and walkers that infest the coral reef 0/18 (Tempest Temple)\n_Task Window Says:_ The crawlers and walkers that infest the reef to the north are far more efficient fisherman than Petran. Take a few of them out so that the fish can survive their trip to the east side of the island.\n_If You Get This Step: Kill update._\n=====================\nStop the sea goblins 0/22 (Tempest Temple)\n_Task Window Says:_ The sea goblins to the west are uniquely adept at fishing and Petran suspects that they are his primary competition. Go reduce their population to improve his chance of finding dinner.\n_it's easiest to pull them to the beach. If you try from the ocean side you can often get huge numbers of adds._\n_They summon!_\n_But if you keep pulling back, they will eventually follow._\n_If You Get This Step: Kill update._\n=====================\nBanish the restless undead 0/20 (Tempest Temple)\n_Task Window Says:_ Petran has a hard time concentrating on his fishing duties with the moaning and groaning of the banshees and zombies that haunt the shipwreck just north of his perch. Reduce their numbers so he can focus on his work.\n_If You Get This Step: Kill update._\n========================================================================\nSTEP #2\n========================================================================\nSilence the hideous sea nagas 0/9 (Tempest Temple)\n_Task Window Says:_ The hideous nagas that intermingle with the sea goblins on the west end of the island are proving to be a problem. Petran is unsure whether the goblins are in service to these sea hags or if the snakelike women are subservient to the smarmy ocean callers. Either way, reducing their numbers can only be advantageous to improving Petran's luck in getting a bite.\n_If You Get This Step: Kill update._\n=====================\nStill the restless elementals 0/10 (Tempest Temple)\n_Task Window Says:_ The unyielding storm that engulfs this island has empowered the previously dormant elementals. These creatures focus the powers of lava and air and make the area inhospitable to sea life. Take out either the air elementals that feed the wild winds or the lava elementals that boil the stilled ponds.\n_If you follow the coast around to the southwest from where you get the quest you'll find enough lava spirits to do this step. They are an easy pull once you move in close enough to avoid the other mobs._\n_If You Get This Step: Kill update - \"a lava spirit\" updates this, as does \"an air spirit\"._\n=====================\nDisrupt the chaotic dervishes 0/9 (Tempest Temple)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: Kill update - the dervishes in the pathway through the mountain._\n========================================================================\nSTEP #3\n========================================================================\nKill a few coral or ocean serpents 0/6 (Tempest Temple)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: Kill update._\n=====================\nTake out the sirens or their seduced pirates 0/6 (Tempest Temple)\n_Task Window Says:_ On the north end of the island is a small band of sirens and the weak-willed pirates that have fallen prey to their alluring song. Clearly these invaders sustain themselves on something and Petran suspects that their diet consists primarily of fish. Turn these creatures into churn to improve Petran's odds of finally catching his own dinner.\n_If you go to the far north at the coral barrier, you can pull the seduced pirates to there._\n_If You Get This Step: Kill update - any \"a seduced \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\" mob counts towards this step._\n=====================\nCrush a few reef crabs 0/6 (Tempest Temple)\n_Task Window Says:_ On the south end of the island is a group of reef crabs that seem suspiciously well fed. Petrans wonders if reducing their population would increase the population of catchable fish.\n_If You Get This Step: Kill update._\n=====================\nKnock some sense into the Wardens and their Treants 0/5 (Tempest Temple)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: Kill update on the floating island. Warning: These mobs are a lot tougher than the general zone population. They tend to hit for the mid-20,000s range._\n=====================\nKill 5 Kedge 0/5 (Tempest Temple)\n_Task Window Says:_ As far as Petran can tell, the unceasing storm that surrounds this island is the work of the kedge arcanists that have taken refuge near the center of the island. Take a few of them out in hopes that it improves the weather and by extension the willingness for schools of delicious fish to swim near the island.\n_If You Get This Step: Kill update in the path through the mountain._\n========================================================================\nSTEP #4\n========================================================================\nSpeak to Petran Searake 0/1 (Tempest Temple)\n_Task Window Says:_ Return to Petran Searake and let him know that you have done everything he has requested of you.\n_If You Get This Step: Hail Petran at the zone-in to complete._\nYou say, 'Hail, Petran Searake'\nPetran Searake smiles contentedly, 'Fine work, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. I'm due for a fine haul now. You're welcome to [leave] whenever you please.'\nPetran Searake has high hopes that fish will start biting soon!\n\n---\n\n**TASK REWARDS**\n\\- 19-21 \"Pieces of Eight\" (group currency)\n1-2% XP for level 99\n- Piece of Eight [item=120483]",
